USERADD(8)                 System Administration                  USERADD(8)

NAME
    useradd - create an account

SYNOPSIS
    useradd UID NAME

DESCRIPTION
    Create the account NAME with user id UID (group 100), and give it a
    home directory, /home/NAME, owned by the account with mode 0700.

    The account is created LOCKED: it has no password that can match, so
    nobody can log in to it until the administrator gives it one with
    passwd UID. Accounts are kept in the sealed account table and last
    across reboots.

SECURITY
    The administrator only.

SEE ALSO
    userdel(8), passwd(1)
